{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0f75822c885108a24e021235574c9669fa9d1ec0ff167a7928e14ddec7d6fe7a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The SDK is published as the npm package @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk, and the README badge indicates Node.js 18 or later."},{"claim_ids":["clm_33c59bb24ed1c40aaf38b73f6837698c1e1c36963690cacaa2a30d6b28f57a1e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Use of the SDK is governed by Anthropic's Commercial Terms of Service, except where a specific component or dependency is covered by a different license noted in that component's LICENSE file."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4d3fe48209850d39a3e5a1ea9305ac5cd7c5017700a8ea0f94d124bdac1f57f1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Using the SDK involves collection of feedback including usage data such as code acceptances or rejections, associated conversation data, and user feedback submitted via the /bug command."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5046bc1ec48c1cc204a01c1960a08b9ec00676d6e23abdf1babedc9e231f0245"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Claude Code SDK has been renamed to the Claude Agent SDK, and a migration guide documents the breaking changes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_713e6e5c1a4ccd01fb1c59046f25e166c4ef7bc6c4bba7ea32060392b269b3c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per its README, the SDK lets developers programmatically build AI agents with Claude Code's capabilities, including understanding codebases, editing files, running commands, and executing complex workflows."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e7af213230dfb03e8514c3cae6f77011b21c00f73a8405985884bc7235cc4ee7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Stated privacy safeguards include limited retention periods for sensitive information, restricted access to user session data, and policies against using feedback for model training."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f61b3142fd74d267d9e7c330a99429e0677c6daf8811a522b930e6fc25bc0c75"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented installation method is npm install @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0f7